{"id": "gsm8k-0000", "mode": "sealed", "key": 1, "doc_id": "gsm_guard90-gsm8k-0000", "text": "To determine how much Janet makes every day at the farmers' market, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of eggs laid per day:**\n   Janet's ducks lay 16 eggs per day.\n\n2. **Determine the number of eggs eaten for breakfast:**\n   Janet eats 3 eggs for breakfast every morning.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of eggs left after breakfast:**\n   \\[\n   16 \\text{ eggs} - 3 \\text{ eggs} = 13 \\text{ eggs}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the number of eggs used to bake muffins for friends:**\n   Janet bakes muffins for her friends using 4 eggs.\n\n5. **Calculate the number of eggs left after baking muffins:**\n   \\[\n   13 \\text{ eggs} - 4 \\text{ eggs} = 9 \\text{ eggs}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the total number of eggs left for sale at the farmers' market:**\n   \\[\n   9 \\text{ eggs}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculate the total revenue from selling the remaining eggs:**\n   Janet sells each egg for $2.\n   \\[\n   9 \\text{ eggs} \\times \\$2/\\text{egg} = \\$18\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Janet makes \\(\\boxed{18}\\) dollars every day at the farmers' market.", "token": "ep1.pGFuTJykHDyEpvkTCt8AWWF2AWJjdFkHO4GaNuEffUNC_l5x-jyU6DnqO4nxJXTZiuEH6ZD9zrfCHWsv3A7HtU4QCzE2DV6ukRRF7Z6WQ_CBoT2ZXiwFtqxk3MAAXFobxWs2GWuqE8Vi6BjsRo_upfksR4kdfWjqb5CVeCzvRKTduMgbls5J2DrBIXyWUiYlR1bwoCwl_u1xBl-eUjW7Xh3Zn0j1l0xA9FqXyNIjFda7YXFWd21GHiw60cOGkaBe1wEJuWuTKcPuyJ7An7bYSkDdztYZGqXAc3ULc1PBR6iQlIz-AP20cQQh4KOE8VT_SzWDdlFbDT_VnhaRDb_xujmEZh6eMIIoLKgYXvp4Y4ZUphWoatfC2UA2TH_JIeawtA_q5EvvdMBNP2ZbqOtLwiHwWNm8IYtRiMO69hp7Y1KZzawPXGF9ekoJukURX5vDvy2Ws9_eI01bZst7vr_rprDOosRXXEsr68WA27-7We3A3-JvsTqSVq9xP5AR4xMlNzYiUZitk1wQzt0Ef0spCqzUVtzx8kARpsoeAtSeYBfl7bQvTTud2P9Hz4NjbU4PmaE6D7Kr7_RjtPFnD2TJ6aupPJ5otvAknY27v_UYFVxj3BAqgAcxWPqFo2NWnZDFAeswe3uE8NM1wu5xNeiDE8iwT_3TduqxbTW5fXapTFxEM-WO4P_coLI4jfsTNKHx3ma15GuBiPYlfF9i5lZQS5TfeB942PRcFBr5xf6HYuz5vL7xwPsFX6z1F4j37hNarUPR6qlepIhL2oSlJklp2a2ikJd1bcFLj09zVq1Z